{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:22:50Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 27, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t## Review: Taiga #10 \u2014 Show how many tasks are left\n2\t\n3\t**Will block:** none.\n4\t\n5\t**Will comment:**\n6\t- `frontend/src/App.css:11` \u2014 `h1`'s `margin-bottom` was tightened from `1.2rem` to `0.3rem` to make room for the new counts line, but `TaskCounts` only renders `!loading`. During the initial loading flash, `AddTask` sits right under `<h1>` with the reduced margin, so the heading-to-input gap briefly shrinks before popping back open once the counts line mounts. It's implemented exactly as `docs/design.md`'s wireframes show, so it's a documented tradeoff rather than a bug \u2014 worth a follow-up if the loading flash turns out to be visually noticeable in practice, not a blocker.\n7\t\n8\t**Worth considering:**\n9\t- No frontend test exists anywhere in this repo (`npm test` isn't even wired up in `package.json`), so `TaskCounts.jsx` ships without one. This is a pre-existing, repo-wide gap this diff didn't introduce or worsen \u2014 not something to hold this change for.\n10\t\n11\tEverything else checks out: `TaskCounts.jsx` matches `docs/design.md` verbatim (props, JSX, `role=\"status\"`, separator), `openCount`/`completedCount` are both derived from `tasks` (not the filtered/sorted view), satisfying the spec's explicit \"true totals, not the current filter\" requirement. Singular/plural logic is correct at 0/1/N independently per bucket. The `#5a646c` contrast claim in the design doc checks out (5.63:1, computed independently). `npm run build` passes. No backend touched, matching both docs' non-goals. No scope creep, no dead code, no stray files left on disk.\n12\t\n13\t**VERDICT: approve-with-followups**", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_0191VoozFBcHAZJURj2PPGHh", "session_id": "744b1940-c4ba-4635-afb0-ac675d200ec2"}}
