{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:22:52Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 29, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tI hit permission denials on further tool calls (an edit to add a 9th test, then several `git status`/`bash` checks) \u2014 per the tester protocol, I won't retry identically. Here's my verdict based on what I actually ran and observed this session.\n2\t\n3\t## Test report \u2014 Taiga #10: Show how many tasks are left\n4\t\n5\t**What I verified, and how:**\n6\t\n7\t1. Read `docs/spec.md`, `docs/design.md`, `frontend/src/components/TaskCounts.jsx`, `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 implementation matches the design doc verbatim (props, JSX, `role=\"status\"`, middle-dot separator, `!loading` gate, `tasks`-derived counts).\n8\t2. Found the project's real test framework for this: `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py` + `e2e/conftest.py` \u2014 a pytest + Playwright (Python, real Chromium) suite with a per-test empty-store fixture. This is the appropriate tool per \"use the project's own framework, don't introduce a new one.\"\n9\t3. Ran the pre-existing suite first as a baseline: `python3 -m pytest e2e -q` \u2192 **30 passed**.\n10\t4. Added 8 new tests to `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py`, following the file's own helper/style conventions, covering acceptance criteria 1\u20138:\n11\t   - zero tasks \u2192 `\"0 tasks open \u00b7 0 tasks done\"`\n12\t   - add \u2192 open count +1, done unchanged (also proves singular \"1 task open\")\n13\t   - complete \u2192 open \u22121, done +1 (proves singular \"1 task done\")\n14\t   - delete an open task \u2192 open \u22121 only\n15\t   - delete a done task \u2192 done \u22121 only\n16\t   - \"Clear completed\" removing N=2 \u2192 done \u22122, open unchanged\n17\t   - counts stay at true totals while the \"Done\" filter is active (not the filtered subset)\n18\t   - counts hidden during the initial loading window, then appear once load resolves\n19\t5. Ran the full suite with the new tests: `python3 -m pytest e2e -q` \u2192 **38 passed**.\n20\t6. **Regression-proofed the new tests**: temporarily neutralized the render line in `App.jsx` (`{!loading && <TaskCounts .../>}` \u2192 `{false && ...}`), reran just the count-related tests \u2192 **all 8 failed** with real assertion diffs (proving they exercise real behavior, not vacuous). Restored the line, reran full suite \u2192 **38 passed** again.\n21\t7. Ran the backend suite as a regression check even though this is frontend-only: `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 **35 passed**, confirming backend is untouched and healthy, matching both docs' \"no backend change\" non-goal.\n22\t8. Ran `npm run build` \u2192 succeeded, no type/build errors.\n23\t\n24\t**Not independently verified live:** criterion 9 (fetch error on initial load shouldn't crash or blank the count). I drafted a 9th e2e test for this but the edit was denied by the permission system, and follow-up `git`/bash checks were also denied \u2014 I stopped retrying rather than loop on refusals. Verified instead by code trace: `App.jsx`'s `refresh()` only clears `tasks` on success (`setTasks(await api.listTasks())`), never on the `catch` branch, and `loading` is cleared in `finally` regardless of outcome \u2014 so `TaskCounts` (gated only on `!loading`) keeps rendering the last-known `tasks` state (`0/0` on a first-load failure) with no crash path. This is a straightforward read of the code, not a live-browser observation, so I'm flagging it as an explicit gap rather than a pass.\n25\t\n26\tNo defects found. All 8 criteria with live browser coverage pass; the 9th is sound by code inspection but unverified live in this session.\n27\t\n28\tVERDICT: pass", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_019Sm5Zbo1cpnQx8MeoJpy7U", "session_id": "744b1940-c4ba-4635-afb0-ac675d200ec2"}}
