als while the \\\"Done\\\" filter is active (not the filtered subset)\\n   - counts hidden during the initial loading window, then appear once load resolves\\n5. Ran the full suite with the new tests: `python3 -m pytest e2e -q` \\u2192 **38 passed**.\\n6. **Regression-proofed the new tests**: temporarily neutralized the render line in `App.jsx` (`{!loading && <TaskCounts .../>}` \\u2192 `{false && ...}`), reran just the count-related tests \\u2192 **all 8 failed** with real assertion diffs (proving they exercise real behavior, not vacuous). Restored the line, reran full suite \\u2192 **38 passed** again.\\n7. Ran the backend suite as a regression check even though this is frontend-only: `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \\u2192 **35 passed**, confirming backend is untouched and healthy, matching both docs' \\\"no backend change\\\" non-goal.\\n8. Ran `npm run build` \\u2192 succeeded, no type/build errors.\\n\\n**Not independently verified live:** criterion 9 (fetch error on initial load shouldn't crash or blank the count). I drafted a 9th e2e test for this but the edit was denied by the permission system, and follow-up `git`/bash checks were also denied \\u2014 I stopped retrying rather than loop on refusals. Verified instead by code trace: `App.jsx`'s `refresh()` only clears `tasks` on success (`setTasks(await api.listTasks())`), never on the `catch` branch, and `loading` is cleared in `finally` regardless of outcome \\u2014 so `TaskCounts` (gated only on `!loading`) keeps rendering the last-known `tasks` state (`0/0` on a first-load failure) with no crash path. This is a straightforward read of the code, not a live-browser observation, so I'm flagging it as an explicit gap rather than a pass.\\n\\nNo defects found. All 8 criteria with live browser coverage pass; the 9th is sound by code inspection but unverified live in this session.\\n\\nVERDICT: pass\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"assistant\", \"block_type\": \"text\", \"session_id\": \"a1a9fb2d-6eda-4780-a0e2-d3742e9e5fcd\"}}\n229:{\"ts\": \"2026-08-17T12:22:07Z\", \"agent\": \"claude\", \"seq\": 229, \"kind\": \"status\", \"text\": \"I hit permission denials on further tool calls (an edit to add a 9th test, then several `git status`/`bash` checks) \\u2014 per the tester protocol, I won't retry identically. Here's my verdict based on what I actually ran and observed this session.\\n\\n## Test report \\u2014 Taiga #10: Show how many tasks are left\\n\\n**What I verified, and how:**\\n\\n1. Read `docs/spec.md`, `docs/design.md`, `frontend/src/components/TaskCounts.jsx`, `frontend/src/App.jsx` \\u2014 implementation matches the design doc verbatim (props, JSX, `role=\\\"status\\\"`, middle-dot separator, `!loading` gate, `tasks`-derived counts).\\n2. Found the project's real test framework for this: `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py` + `e2e/conftest.py` \\u2014 a pytest + Playwright (Python, real Chromium) suite with a per-test empty-store fixture. This is the appropriate tool per \\\"use the project's own framework, don't introduce a new one.\\\"\\n3. Ran the pre-existing suite first as a baseline: `python3 -m pytest e2e -q` \\u2192 **30 passed**.\\n4. Added 8 new tests to `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py`, following the file's own helper/style conventions, covering acceptance criteria 1\\u20138:\\n   - zero tasks \\u2192 `\\\"0 tasks open \\u00b7 0 tasks done\\\"`\\n   - add \\u2192 open count +1, done unchanged (also proves singular \\\"1 task open\\\")\\n   - complete \\u2192 open \\u22121, done +1 (proves singular \\\"1 task done\\\")\\n   - delete an open task \\u2192 open \\u22121 only\\n   - delete a done task \\u2192 done \\u22121 only\\n   - \\\"Clear completed\\\" removing N=2 \\u2192 done \\u22122, open unchanged\\n   - counts stay at true totals while the \\\"Done\\\" filter is active (not the filtered subset)\\n   - counts hidden during the initial loading window, then appear once load resolves\\n5. Ran the full suite with the new tests: `python3 -m pytest e2e -q` \\u2192 **38 passed**.\\n6. **Regression-proofed the new tests**: temporarily neutralized the render line in `App.jsx` (`{!loading && <TaskCounts .../>}` \\u2192 `{false && ...}`), reran just the count-related tests \\u2192 **all 8 failed** with real assertion diffs (proving they exercise real behavior, not vacuous). Restored the line, reran full suite \\u2192 **38 passed** again.\\n7. Ran the backend suite as a regression check even though this is frontend-only: `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \\u2192 **35 passed**, confirming backend is untouched and healthy, matching both docs' \\\"no backend change\\\" non-goal.\\n8. Ran `npm run build` \\u2192 succeeded, no type/build errors.\\n\\n**Not independently verified live:** criterion 9 (fetch error on initial load shouldn't crash or blank the count). I drafted a 9th e2e test for this but the edit was denied by the permission system, and follow-up `git`/bash checks were also denied \\u2014 I stopped retrying rather than loop on refusals. Verified instead by code trace: `App.jsx`'s `refresh()` only clears `tasks` on success (`setTasks(await api.listTasks())`), never on the `catch` branch, and `loading` is cleared in `finally` regardless of outcome \\u2014 so `TaskCounts` (gated only on `!loading`) keeps rendering the last-known `tasks` state (`0/0` on a first-load failure) with no crash path. This is a straightforward read of the code, not a live-browser observation, so I'm flagging it as an explicit gap rather than a pass.\\n\\nNo defects found. All 8 criteria with live browser coverage pass; the 9th is sound by code inspection but unverified live in this session.\\n\\nVERDICT: pass\", \"meta\": {\"native_type\": \"result\", \"subtype\": \"success\", \"session_id\": \"a1a9fb2d-6eda-4780-a0e2-d3742e9e5fcd\", \"is_error\": false, \"total_cost_usd\": 1.2561816000000001}}", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01AUL5cRVBoCufC2TGABHH8e", "session_id": "744b1940-c4ba-4635-afb0-ac675d200ec2"}}
