{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:23:17Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 61, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tSpec written to `docs/spec.md` for Taiga #10. Summary:\n2\t\n3\t**Triage:** Feature, frontend-only \u2014 no backend change needed since the full task list is already in `App.jsx` state; counts are a pure client-side derivation, same pattern as the existing `completedCount` at `App.jsx:38`.\n4\t\n5\t**Key acceptance criteria:** open/done counts always visible (even at 0), correct singular/plural grammar at exactly 1, stay correct across add/complete/delete/clear-completed with no reload, hidden during initial load, and counts reflect true totals rather than whatever the current filter has scrolled into view.\n6\t\n7\t**Flagged assumption (proceeding on it, not blocking):** the count should show true totals independent of the `TaskFilter` selection, not the filtered subset \u2014 since \"how many are left\" is about actual task state, not the current view.\n8\t\n9\tNext stage is ux-designer, which should read `docs/spec.md` to produce `docs/design.md` (exact copy/wording and placement of the new count element).", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01QuhsQKA6yoai3XaLXLB9Se", "session_id": "744b1940-c4ba-4635-afb0-ac675d200ec2"}}
