{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:23:20Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 65, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tThe frontend implementation is complete and verified, but I hit a blocker on the final documentation step.\n2\t\n3\t**Implementation (done, verified):**\n4\t- `frontend/src/components/TaskCounts.jsx` (new) \u2014 renders open/done counts with independent singular/plural grammar, `role=\"status\"` live region.\n5\t- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 imports `TaskCounts`, adds `openCount`, renders `{!loading && <TaskCounts open={openCount} done={completedCount} />}` under `<h1>`.\n6\t- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 tightened `h1` bottom margin, added `.task-counts` rule (AA-passing `#5a646c`).\n7\t\n8\tAll three match `docs/design.md` verbatim \u2014 no deviations. `npm run build` succeeds (verified this session). `npm test` fails with \"Missing script: test\" \u2014 a pre-existing gap (no test framework installed anywhere in the repo), not something this change introduced. `npm run lint` (oxlint) isn't in this session's Bash allowlist, so it wasn't run \u2014 the reviewer stage should run it.\n9\t\n10\t**Blocked:** The `Write` call for `docs/implementation.md` was denied twice (`.claude/settings.json` lists `Write(./docs/**)` as allowed, so this is likely a session-specific denial rather than a policy mismatch). I could not write the handoff file myself. Here is its complete, ready-to-apply content \u2014 the next attempt should write this verbatim to `/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/implementation.md`:\n11\t\n12\t```markdown\n13\t# Implementation: Show how many tasks are left\n14\t\n15\tTaiga #10 \u00b7 reads `docs/spec.md`, `docs/design.md`\n16\t\n17\t## Scope\n18\t\n19\tFrontend-only, exactly as designed. No backend changes.\n20\t\n21\t## Files changed\n22\t\n23\t- **New:** `frontend/src/components/TaskCounts.jsx` \u2014 presentational component,\n24\t  takes `open`/`done` integer props, renders one `<p className=\"task-counts\"\n25\t  role=\"status\">` with independent singular/plural grammar per bucket, per\n26\t  `docs/design.md`'s spec verbatim.\n27\t- **`frontend/src/App.jsx`:**\n28\t  - Import `TaskCounts` (line 3, alphabetical with the other component\n29\t    imports).\n30\t  - `openCount = tasks.filter((t) => !t.done).length` added next to the\n31\t    existing `completedCount` (line 39-40) \u2014 both derive from `tasks`, never\n32\t    `visibleTasks`/`sortedTasks`.\n33\t  - `{!loading && <TaskCounts open={openCount} done={completedCount} />}`\n34\t    rendered directly under `<h1>Tasks</h1>` (line 56), above `AddTask`.\n35\t- **`frontend/src/App.css`:**\n36\t  - `h1` bottom margin tightened from `1.2rem` to `0.3rem` so the counts line\n37\t    sits snug under the title.\n38\t  - New `.task-counts` rule added next to `.empty, .loading` (same \"muted\n39\t    secondary text\" category): `margin: 0 0 1.2rem; font-size: 0.95rem;\n40\t    color: #5a646c;` \u2014 the AA-contrast-passing color computed in\n41\t    `docs/design.md` (5.63:1 on the page background), not a reuse of the\n42\t    existing `#6b7780` (which the design doc found fails at 4.28:1).\n43\t\n44\tNo other files touched. `frontend/src/api.js` untouched \u2014 no new request.\n45\t\n46\t## Deviations from design\n47\t\n48\tNone. Component shape, wiring, CSS, and placement all match `docs/design.md`\n49\tverbatim.\n50\t\n51\t## Verification\n52\t\n53\t- **Build:** `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2014 succeeds, no errors:\n54\t  ```\n55\t  \u2713 22 modules transformed.\n56\t  \u2713 built in 109ms\n57\t  ```\n58\t- **Tests:** `cd frontend && npm test` \u2014 fails with `npm error Missing\n59\t  script: \"test\"`. This is a **pre-existing gap**, not introduced by this\n60\t  change: `frontend/package.json` has no `test` script and no testing\n61\t  library (`@testing-library/react`, `vitest`, etc.) is installed anywhere in\n62\t  the repo (`node_modules/.bin/` only has `oxlint`, `vite`, `rolldown`,\n63\t  `nanoid`). There is no existing frontend test to use as a precedent for\n64\t  this component, and installing a test framework is out of scope for a\n65\t  single-component feature diff per the \"minimal diff\" discipline \u2014 flagging\n66\t  for reviewer/product-manager rather than silently skipping.\n67\t- **Lint:** not run \u2014 `oxlint` is not in this session's Bash allowlist\n68\t  (`.claude/settings.json` permits `npm run build*`/`npm run dev*`/`npm\n69\t  test*` but not `npm run lint*`, and direct `node_modules/.bin/oxlint`\n70\t  invocation is likewise outside the allowlist). Reviewer has broader Bash\n71\t  access and should run `npm run lint` to confirm.\n72\t- **Manual/visual check:** not run (no browser tool in this dispatch's\n73\t  toolset). Reviewer's pass should exercise: zero tasks, exactly one task in\n74\t  each bucket, add/complete/delete/clear-completed transitions, loading\n75\t  state (count absent), and error state (count keeps last-known values) \u2014\n76\t  matching the states enumerated in `docs/design.md`.\n77\t\n78\t## How to run and verify\n79\t\n80\t```bash\n81\tcd backend  && python3 -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload   # terminal 1\n82\tcd frontend && npm run dev                                 # terminal 2\n83\t```\n84\tOpen the app: the counts line reads e.g. \"3 tasks open \u00b7 2 tasks done\"\n85\tunder the \"Tasks\" heading, updates immediately on add/complete/delete/clear\n86\tcompleted with no reload, and disappears only during the initial load.\n87\t\n88\t## Known limitations\n89\t\n90\t- No automated test coverage for `TaskCounts` or the new `openCount`\n91\t  derivation \u2014 see \"Tests\" above. The logic is a one-line pure filter\n92\t  (`tasks.filter((t) => !t.done).length`), directly parallel to the\n93\t  already-untested `completedCount` on the line above it, so this follows\n94\t  existing project precedent rather than introducing a new gap in test\n95\t  discipline.\n96\t```\n97\t\n98\tEverything else (the actual code diff) is applied and verified in this session.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Lh333oq7zaaYnQYdWtazsP", "session_id": "744b1940-c4ba-4635-afb0-ac675d200ec2"}}
